.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt SLEEP 1
.Os OxideBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm sleep
.Nd wait for a time
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar number Ns Op Ar unit
.Op Ar ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
waits for the total of its arguments, then exits.
Each is a number of seconds, which may have a fraction, optionally followed by
a unit:
.Cm s
(seconds),
.Cm m
(minutes),
.Cm h
(hours) or
.Cm d
(days).
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Wait a minute and a half:
.Dl sleep 1m 30
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr nanosleep 2
.Sh STANDARDS
.Nm
conforms to
.St -p1003.1-2008 ;
fractions, units and more than one argument are extensions, as on
.Fx .
.Sh HISTORY
A
.Nm
command appeared in
.At v4 .
